 * ## Module Organization
 * - **InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class)**: Available application-wide
 * - **@Singleton**: Single instance shared across app
 * - **Abstract class**: Dagger/Hilt generates implementation code
 *
 * ## When to Use @Binds vs @Provides
 *
 * ### Use @Binds (This Module)
 * When binding interface to single implementation:
 * ```kotlin
 * @Binds
 * abstract fun bindRepository(impl: DefaultRepo): RepoInterface
 * ```
 * Benefits:
 * - More efficient (no method body, Dagger generates code)
 * - Clearer intent (simple interface mapping)
 *
 * ### Use @Provides
 * When you need:
 * - Multiple implementations:
 *   ```kotlin
 *   @Provides @Named("remote")
 *   fun provideRemoteRepo(...): Repository = RemoteRepositoryImpl(...)
 *
 *   @Provides @Named("local")
 *   fun provideLocalRepo(...): Repository = LocalRepositoryImpl(...)
 *   ```
 *
 * - Complex construction logic:
 *   ```kotlin
 *   @Provides
 *   fun provideRepository(
 *       dao: Dao,
 *       api: Api,
 *       prefs: Prefs
 *   ): Repository {
 *       return if (BuildConfig.USE_MOCK) {
 *           MockRepository()
 *       } else {
 *           DefaultRepository(dao, api, prefs)
 *       }
 *   }
 *   ```
 *
 * - Return type different from implementation:
 *   ```kotlin
 *   @Provides
 *   fun provideExecutor(): Executor = Executors.newSingleThreadExecutor()
 *   ```
 *
 * ## Scopes
 * - **@Singleton**: One instance per app (use for stateless repositories)
 * - **@ActivityRetainedScoped**: Survives config changes
 * - **@ActivityScoped**: New instance per Activity
 * - **@ViewModelScoped**: Scoped to ViewModel lifecycle
